{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:94514",
  "title": "Important: freerdp security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-04 09:10:56"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-07 00:12:48"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "FreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), released under the Apache license. The xfreerdp client can connect to RDP servers such as Microsoft Windows machines, xrdp, and VirtualBox.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via uninitialized progressive tile handling (CVE-2026-109242)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP 3.0.0-beta1 before 3.32.0 Use-After-Free via Smartcard Connect (CVE-2026-109676)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Unauthenticated keystroke injection via premature input dispatch (CVE-2026-110838)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via file descriptor exhaustion in serial device handling (CVE-2026-110830)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap-based buffer overflow during MP3 audio decoding (CVE-2026-110837)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via unbounded memory consumption during RDPDR reassembly (CVE-2026-110833)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via grayscale JPEG clipboard conversion (CVE-2026-110839)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via memory exhaustion in NLA frame parser (CVE-2026-111378)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Arbitrary code execution via crafted persistent cache file (CVE-2026-111379)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via crafted persistent cache file (CVE-2026-111381)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via crafted display frames (CVE-2026-111382)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds write in NTLM authentication (CVE-2026-111880)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: heap buffer overflow in server rdpsnd via crafted audio formats (CVE-2026-114045)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Rebase FreeRDP to 3.32.2 or newer [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-277442)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
